WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.270
ADDIE helps course creators move from a learning need to a designed experience,

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.053
built materials, delivered course, and evaluated results.

00:00:08.053 --> 00:00:13.223
It gives the work a practical rhythm: analyze the problem, design the experience,

00:00:13.223 --> 00:00:17.199
develop the materials, implement the delivery, and evaluate what happened.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:20.381
Each phase answers a different kind of question.

00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:24.755
Strong eLearning uses ADDIE to clarify the problem before creating screens.

00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:28.731
The Analyze phase identifies audience, context, constraints, and performance needs.

00:00:28.731 --> 00:00:33.106
The Design phase turns those findings into objectives, structure, practice, assessment,

00:00:33.106 --> 00:00:35.094
narration, visuals, and accessibility plans.

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:40.661
The Develop phase builds purposeful assets instead of producing media for its own sake.

00:00:40.661 --> 00:00:42.649
Implementation makes the course operational.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:46.626
It covers publishing, LMS configuration, learner access, tracking, communication, support,

00:00:46.626 --> 00:00:47.421
and rollout.

00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:51.795
Evaluation closes the loop by looking at feedback, data, workplace results,

00:00:51.795 --> 00:00:52.988
and improvement opportunities.

00:00:52.988 --> 00:00:56.965
A course is not truly finished just because it launches;

00:00:56.965 --> 00:01:00.146
it becomes more useful when evidence informs maintenance.

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:03.725
The goal is not to follow a template mechanically.

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:08.497
The goal is to create courses that learners can understand, complete, apply,

00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:09.690
and improve from.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.474
ADDIE should support judgment, not replace it.

00:01:12.474 --> 00:01:16.052
Use it to ask better questions, make better decisions,

00:01:16.052 --> 00:01:18.836
and keep stakeholders aligned around learner outcomes.

00:01:18.836 --> 00:01:22.415
A durable ADDIE practice is clear, iterative, and evidence-informed.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.392
It prevents tool-first development, content dumps, weak assessments, accessibility surprises,

00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:27.585
and unsupported rollouts.

00:01:27.585 --> 00:01:28.380
Most importantly,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.152
it keeps course creation focused on the learner and the real work

00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:35.140
the learner needs to perform.
